Chapter: BvtFighterLoot
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeFighter
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtWorkerDay
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 The first lot the provisioner (vendor 0) holds whose item some shop bids on, or -1.
  bfl-sellable : CompositeGame, TownLive, Integer -> Integer
  bfl-sellable (owner) (t) (serial) = if serial == 0 then -1
    else let goods = owner.vendor.currency.world.goods
    in if ep-lot-amount goods serial >= 1 & cgf-buyer-of t (ep-lot-item goods serial) 0 -1 0 >= 0 then serial
    else bfl-sellable owner t (ep-lot-next goods serial)
 On the founded Britain, a corpse one tile east of the fighter holds a sellable provisioner lot. With leg and took set,
 answers a code: 1 the lot passed to the fighter's actor, 2 it left the corpse, 4 the fighter carried no wares before and
 does after; a negative step when the scenario could not be built.
  bfl-loot : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  bfl-loot (leg) (took) = when bwd-founded 0
    is Err (_) -> -1
    is Ok (owner) -> when owner.fighter
      is None -> -2
      is Just (c) -> when owner.town
        is None -> -3
        is Just (t) -> let w = owner.vendor.currency.world
          in let at = bfl-sellable owner t (ep-lot-first w.goods (list-at owner.vendor.vendors 0).actor)
          in if at < 0 then -4
          else let lot = ep-lot w.goods at
          in when world-get owner.checkpoint.game.world c.serial
            is Err (_) -> -5
            is Ok (m) -> when world-create owner.items.world (WorldObject { serial = 0, kind = 2, x = m.x + 1, y = m.y, z = m.z, graphic = #2006, hue = 0, container = 0, amount = 1, health = 0 })
              is Err (_) -> -6
              is Ok (corpse) -> when world-get owner.items.world lot.serial
                is Err (_) -> -7
                is Ok (o) -> when world-update owner.items.world (__record-set (__record-set (__record-set o "container" corpse) "x" 60) "y" 80)
                  is Err (_) -> -8
                  is Ok (_) -> let before = cgf-loot c t
                    in let a = __record-set c "leg" leg
                    in let b = __record-set c "took" took
                    in let looted = cg-fighter-loot owner c owner.checkpoint.game
                    in let mine = (ep-lot w.goods at).actor == c.fighter.producer.actor
                    in let left = when world-get owner.items.world lot.serial is Err (_) -> False is Ok (after) -> after.container /= corpse
                    in (if mine then 1 else 0) + (if left then 2 else 0) + (if before == 0 & cgf-loot c t == 1 then 4 else 0)
 The vendor bidding most for an item: fish (9) is the fishmonger's alone (UOAIX-167), and nothing bids on an item no
 shop buys (the spell scroll, 116, which only the scribe makes).
  bfl-buyers : Integer -> Integer
  bfl-buyers (unused) = when bwd-founded 0
    is Err (_) -> -1
    is Ok (owner) -> when owner.town
      is None -> -2
      is Just (t) -> (if cgf-buyer-of t 9 0 -1 0 == bb-fishmonger then 1 else 0) + (if cgf-buyer-of t 116 0 -1 0 < 0 then 2 else 0)
  bvt-fighter-loot : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-fighter-loot (unused) = act
    k <- bfl-loot 4 1
    a <- bvt-check ("after a kill (leg 4, the kill taken) the fighter loots a corpse beside it: the lot passes to its actor and leaves the corpse, and it now carries wares to sell (UOAIX-140 e, code " & show k & ")") (k == 7)
    h <- bfl-loot 2 0
    b <- bvt-check ("a fighter still hunting (leg 2, no kill) loots nothing: the lot stays in the corpse with its owner (code " & show h & ")") (h == 0)
    n <- bfl-buyers 0
    c <- bvt-check ("the fighter sells each ware to the shop bidding most: fish to the fishmonger, and no shop for an item none buys (code " & show n & ")") (n == 3)
    a + b + c
  end
